#!/usr/bin/env zsh
# cheatsheet: print the Claude and tmux session commands and their shortcuts.
# Rendered with glow when it is installed, paged when printing to a terminal.

emulate -L zsh

local md
md=$(cat <<'MD'
# Claude sessions

Sessions you can find again. The slug is the tmux window name *and* the
Claude session name. A bare number is a ticket: `2108` is `eng-2108`
(`CL_TICKET_PREFIX` changes the prefix).

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `cl <name> [prompt]` | New session named `<name>` in a window of the same name, with `prompt` as the first message |
| `cl <name>` | Switch to its window if open; otherwise resume it where it started |
| `cl <name> <prompt>` | Same, and send `prompt` as the next message |
| `cl -d DIR <name> ...` | Start a new session in `DIR` instead of the current directory |
| `cl -i <name> ...` | Same, but in the current window, renamed `<name>` while claude runs (`clw -i`, `clr -i` too) |
| `cl` | Pick a known session with fzf, most recent first |
| `cl -l` | List known sessions; `*` marks ones with an open window |
| `clw <ticket>` | `cl <ticket> "what are the next steps for eng-<ticket>?"` |
| `clr <ticket>` | `cl <ticket> "review prs open for eng-<ticket>; don't run checks"` |
| `claude-pick` | fzf over *running* Claude sessions in tmux, with a pane preview; jumps to the chosen pane |
| `cc` | `claude --continue`: most recent session in this directory |
| `cr [name]` | `claude --resume`: the session picker, or a named session |

Inside Claude: `/rename <name>` names the current session, `/resume <name>`
switches to another, `/branch` forks the conversation.

# tmux

Prefix is `C-y` (also `C-space`).

| Keys | What it does |
|---|---|
| `prefix C-c` | Pick a running Claude session (`claude-pick` in a popup) |
| `prefix t` | Shell in a popup |
| `prefix c` | New window |
| `prefix C` | New window, prompting for a command |
| `prefix "` | Rename the current window |
| `prefix (` / `prefix {` | Previous / next window |
| `prefix <` / `prefix >` | Move the window left / right |
| `prefix s` / `prefix v` | Split below / right, in the current directory |
| `C-h` `C-j` `C-k` `C-l` | Move between panes (and vim splits) |
| `prefix V` | Copy mode; `v` selects, `y` yanks, `Enter` copies to the clipboard |
| `prefix P` / `prefix Y` | Paste from / copy to the system clipboard |
| `prefix r` | Reload `tmux.conf` |

Window names set by `cl` never change. Other windows show the running
command, or the directory name when it is a shell.

Where things live: `~/.local/state/cl/sessions` (the `cl` ledger),
`~/.claude/sessions/` (Claude's registry of running processes),
`~/.claude/projects/` (transcripts).
MD
)

if (( $+commands[glow] )); then
  if [[ -t 1 ]]; then
    print -r -- "$md" | glow -p -w "${COLUMNS:-100}" -
  else
    print -r -- "$md" | glow -w 100 -
  fi
else
  print -r -- "$md"
fi
